igher-rank duality groups?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:71dcb4bfc2ee8e354658bf0873f3c9c67b66636cf479330d0fe2720bd4b46c0f","title":"What excludes the infinite anomaly-compatible su(N)⊕u(1) families, including N<13 descendants for which the specific su(13) local enhancement does not apply? The source leaves both the common obstruction and the role of quadratic charge dependence unresolved.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:717c3b24dd383b50ffb1398fb7762cf1c7e2dfe9ff74cf6661a73e32dbba7bfe","title":"Is the two-dimensional quartically interacting real scalar theory on Snyder-de Sitter space renormalizable at one loop for small curvature and noncommutativity, and how do these deformations affect its renormalization group flow?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:71ab4bfb7bb6955069e31ba2d0081430dfcbff81121205477ca0323c62c87c43","title":"Which source orientations and internal geometries permit AdS or Minkowski solutions? The argument compares internal curvature traced along directions 5 and 6 with signed source contributions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0073"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:71d64413f10c18cf972d71f6ce6fe855c61223bbe038ef70d63b20518cea4d97","title":"What cosmological consequences follow if parity or CP is a fundamental gauge symmetry broken spontaneously at low energy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0078"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:717b9accb34f11d8453230a5531898b32f8d29e4adbb2f0d3a4261cf57306e3d","title":"Can a neutral, smooth, horizonless massive object preserve four-dimensional Lorentz invariance and serve as an AdS-to-de Sitter uplift